  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#script-processing-empty\r\n\r\n> If the element has no src attribute, and its child nodes, if any, consist only of comment nodes and empty Text nodes, then return\\. The script is not executed\\.\r\n\r\nThis seems overly complicated. It says that we'll try to execute a script with, e.g., element children. Maybe this is a holdover from when the script processing model meant to support non-JS script types?\r\n\r\nI'd like this to just check if the child text content is not the empty string. Will require some noodling to see if this is an observable difference and if so write tests.\r\n\r\n(Worth noting, we could go further and e.g. check that the child text content contains more than just ASCII whitespace. Or Unicode whitespace, for that matter! But that crosses a line into depending on the fact that the JS spec will do nothing for programs with only whitespace in them, and I think we should not go that far, even though it's a pretty safe assumption.)",
